From 5a51f0166ae6b1d1199c91a6d78dfe8813d3b62d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MaySoMusician <maysomusician@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:24:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/22] 🐛 fix(openai): use one attempt and a one-hour timeout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

LLM calls are never retried automatically, and every OpenAI-compatible
request gets a one-hour timeout: the instrumentation installs undici's
fetch with a one-hour dispatcher globally, and clients keep using that
global fetch so the SSRF guard for user-supplied endpoints still wraps it.
The guarded connections get the same one-hour idle timeouts. Runners
without the instrumentation fall back to an explicit undici fetch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <claude@anthropic.com.invalid>
