From a731d3d94cb155b8f1ec72de46be194f66679fea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MaySoMusician <maysomusician@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:25:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/22] ✨ feat(agent): keep tools explicitly user-controlled
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

No tool reaches a run unless the agent turned it on or the runtime adds it:

- No builtin is always on. The activator, Skills and Verify are ordinary,
  visible tools an agent turns on itself.
- Agent mode uses the same opt-in rule as Chat and Custom: an untouched
  builtin, connector or builtin skill is off, and every entry the agent
  turned on joins the toolset directly. Nothing is discovered by default.
- The activator, and with it deferred runtime tools and on-demand
  connectors, exists only when the agent turned it on.
- Connecting a connector from an agent turns it on for that agent.
- The agent-account and MCP-events tools are allowed but not defaults.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <claude@anthropic.com.invalid>
