From b2b6be7c33d950319e3e9137492c726606c706b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MaySoMusician <maysomusician@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:33:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] ✨ feat(ui): keep editors plain text
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every editor is a plain-text editor: no lists, code blocks, math, tables,
headings or quotes, no Markdown typing shortcuts, no Ctrl+B/I/U, no Markdown
paste conversion, and no formatting toolbars or rich slash blocks. Markdown is
kept exactly as typed: the plain-text plugin reads `markdown` documents as raw
lines and writes them back verbatim, and turns stray rich nodes (formatted
text, headings, quotes, LiteXML blocks from agents) back into Markdown source.

Inline chips (mentions, skills, tools, topic / document / file references)
and image, video and file attachments stay. The message edit dialog loads the
saved editor data again, so chips come back there too; saved data a plain
editor can't show falls back to the text instead of opening empty.

Pages the user can't write (no permission, view access, locked by someone
else, view-only room), the room-sync preview and the skill viewer render the
stored Markdown richly instead.

Paste conversion can no longer be turned on, so Settings > Conversation >
Sending drops its switch, along with its settings-search entry and skeleton
row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <claude@anthropic.com.invalid>
